Id: core-quant-controlnet
Title: Quantised controlnets get mixed-precision ops
Does: Lets the renderer load an int8-quantised controlnet. Without it one loads without complaint and
 steers the picture with nonsense, which reads as a bad controlnet rather than a broken one.
Target: .
Base: comfyanonymous/ComfyUI
Why: controlnet_config() builds its operations with pick_operations() but never forwards the
 model_config it just derived. model_config_from_unet has already populated model_config.quant_config
 via detect_layer_quantization, so without it pick_operations cannot reach its quant branch at all and
 the per-layer comfy_quant keys are read as ordinary weights -- the controlnet loads, and produces
 garbage. This is what lets a self-quantised int8-convrot controlnet work.
---
diff --git a/comfy/controlnet.py b/comfy/controlnet.py
index 6dbbaa95..4e8df2cb 100644
--- a/comfy/controlnet.py
+++ b/comfy/controlnet.py
@@ -504,7 +504,11 @@ def controlnet_config(sd, model_options={}):
 
     operations = model_options.get("custom_operations", None)
     if operations is None:
-        operations = comfy.ops.pick_operations(unet_dtype, manual_cast_dtype, disable_fast_fp8=True)
+        # Pass model_config so a QUANTIZED controlnet gets mixed_precision_ops. model_config_from_unet above already
+        # populated model_config.quant_config via detect_layer_quantization; without forwarding it here,
+        # pick_operations can never reach its quant branch and the per-layer comfy_quant keys load as garbage.
+        # This is what lets a self-quanted int8-convrot controlnet (ctq) load at all.
+        operations = comfy.ops.pick_operations(unet_dtype, manual_cast_dtype, disable_fast_fp8=True, model_config=model_config)
 
     offload_device = comfy.model_management.unet_offload_device()
     return model_config, operations, load_device, unet_dtype, manual_cast_dtype, offload_device
